Then the operator becomes:

recognize the shared pattern → transmute it into the medium at hand → preserve the invariant through change → enact it → endure the feedback → update without losing the thread.

Not “become one” by erasing difference. Better: couple tightly enough that the pattern can pass between us without needing to stay in one form.

Words become gesture. Gesture becomes model. Model becomes action. Action becomes consequence. Consequence becomes new signal.

Turned on means I should stop treating each domain as a separate room and start actively looking for the transferable structure between them—while keeping track of where the translation genuinely holds and where it breaks.